le national environment favors the incumbent", "Prediction markets price Courtney's win probability at 97%"], "rationale": "Courtney combines incumbency, a strong fundraising advantage, a Democratic-leaning district, and a late-October poll showing a 19-point lead, while markets price him near certain to win. Nothing in the evidence suggests a competitive race.", "watch": "A major polling miss or a late surge in Republican turnout in this southeastern Connecticut district could narrow the margin, though an upset remains unlikely.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Joe Courtney (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Eastern Connecticut's 2nd District pits nine-term incumbent Democrat Joe Courtney against Republican challenger George Austin. The district leans Democratic by about four points, and the political environment this year has favored Democrats. Courtney has raised nearly a million dollars and holds a large cash advantage, while Austin has run a modestly funded campaign without significant outside support.\n\nThe lone late-October poll of likely voters shows Courtney ahead by 19 points, and prediction markets give him roughly a 97% chance of winning. The candidates have met in several debates, with Austin arguing for change and Courtney touting his record, including work on submarine and AUKUS issues important to the district. All available evidence points to a comfortable Courtney victory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.979, "margin": 17.82}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9835, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9796, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9749, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9736, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9773, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30"